        int a = 10;
        int b = 20;

        System.out.println(a < b);
    }
}

Outputtrue
Explanation: The < operator checks whether a is less than b; since 10 < 20, the result is trueTpyes of Relational operators in JavaEqual To Operator (==)The Equal To (==) operator is used to check whether two operands have the same value. It returns true if both operands are equal; otherwise, it returns false.Returns true when both operands have equal values. Commonly used in conditional statements for comparison.Syntax:operand1 == operand2
